            <ArticleTitle>Endovascular management of symptomatic cerebral aneurysm thromboembolism due to pre-aneurysmal arterial stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2050313X17730263</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/2050313X17730263</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Pre-aneurysmal internal carotid steno-occlusive disease resulting in cerebral intra-aneurysmal thrombosis and subsequent embolic infarction has not been previously described.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Antithrombotic treatment for dissolution of the thrombus and pre-aneurysmal stent angioplasty followed by Pipeline embolization flow diverter placement through the aneurysm is a safe and feasible management option.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
